Variants: #label constructors, match with a record of handlers, options and pairs from std.
$[Import* std]
$[# {area s} {match s {. circle {^ {r} {* 3.0 {* r r}}} rect {^ {wh} {* {.w wh} {.h wh}}}}}]
${area {#circle 1.0}} ${area {#rect {. w 2.0 h 3.0}}}
expect: 3.0
expect: 6.0
${map {' {#circle 2.0} {#rect {. w 1.0 h 1.0}}} area}
expect: [12.0, 1.0]
${= {#a 1} {#a 1}} ${= {: {#a 1} {Variant {' {Field "a" Int} {Field "b" Int}}}} {#b 1}}
expect: true
expect: false
${#tag 3} ${#unit K::unit}
expect: #tag(3)
expect: #unit
Options are ordinary variants:
${withDefault {some 4} 0} ${withDefault none 0} ${caseOption {some 1} {^ {} "none"} str}
expect: 4
expect: 0
expect: "1"
A wrapper around match keeps its constrained type:
$[# {dispatch v h} {match v h}]
${dispatch {#left 3} {. left {^ {x} {+ x 1}} right {^ {s} 0}}}
expect: 4
Pairs are records:
${pair 1 "a"} ${first {second {pair 1 {pair 2 3}}}}
expect: {first: 1, second: "a"}
expect: 2
A single-alternative variant is a distinct (tagged) type:
$[# meters #meters]
${match {meters 3} {. meters {^ {m} {* m 2}}}}
expect: 6
